ver 6
16 July 2026
Chris Bouchard

* python script to generate quenched lattice QCD gauge fields
* user interface via generate.py
  - specify action (W = Wilson, WR = Wilson with rectangle improvement)
  - to tadpole improve, add "_T" to end of action
  - while tadpole improving, u0 is initialized to the value of the u0 parameter (1 for a
    cold start) and is periodically recalculated from the running average plaquette
    (controlled by Nu0_step, Nu0_avg) and used in the Metropolis updates from then on;
    watch the printed "u0 progression" to see when it has stabilised
  - to freeze u0 once stabilised (production/measurement phase), continue the run with
    the same action string, the u0 parameter set to the stabilised value, and freeze_u0
    set to True, so it is never recalculated again regardless of Nu0_step/Ncfg; do not
    drop the "_T" suffix mid-chain, since the action string also names the output
    directory and switching it will make generate.py look for the previous configuration
    in the wrong place
  - each configuration's u0 (the value actually used to generate it) is logged to
    <dir_name>/u0_<dir_name>.dat as it is saved, and is read back automatically by
    action_v_cfg.py via lattice_collection.fn_load_u0_log(); this is required to get a
    correct tadpole-improved action out of action_v_cfg.py, since evaluating the action
    with the wrong u0 does not reproduce thermalization
* helper functions and classes in gauge_latticeqcd.py and lattice_collection.py
  includes code to update the lattices and perform measurments.
* incorporates Panagiotis Stylianou's updates to original code including:
  - improved generation of updates via SU(2) matrices
  - each Metropolis hit draws its own fresh random SU(3) update matrix (rather than
    drawing from a pre-built pool of Nmatrix matrices), so there is no longer any
    Nmatrix parameter to size relative to Ncfg/Nhits; the matrix, or its conjugate
    transpose with equal probability (required for detailed balance), is used each time
  - use of multiprocessing
  - the addition of measurement code for several observables
* adds calculation of lattice spacing based on beta
* analysis scripts:
  - action_v_cfg.py: calculates action for specified range of existing configurations;
    useful for tracking thermalization
  - plaq_v_cfg.py: calculates avg plaquette for specified range of existing configurations;
    useful for tracking thermalization
  - autocorr.py: calculates autocorrelation over a specified range of configurations; 
    uses the output of action_v_cfg.py as input
  - topo.py: calculation of topological charge over a specified range of configurations 
* ver5, 27 Sep 2025: 
  - corrected calculation of staples in gauge_latticeqcd.py
  - removed default use of multicore
* ver6, 16 Jul 2026
  - added calculation of topological charge script, topo.py
  - topological charge now defaults to use of clover term, the calculation of which has 
    been added to gauge_latticeqcd.py
To do:
* optimize (better numba implementation, ...)
* add gradient flow and scale-setting measurement code to determine lattice spacing
